A||N||18||GT-maniac||Differences between GT and SE noses ?||||1||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||11-29-2001||02:41 PM||||I'm looking at possibly replacing the damaged nose on my 87 GT with one from an 86 SE. Are these fascia's identical ?. I've noticed the 85 and 87 fascias are different. Are they're mounting differences as well ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hartz||11-29-2001||02:50 PM||||Other than the side moulding (ribbed vs. rounded) how are the '85 and '87 aero noses different?  I've never noticed that before, and am curious.<P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com||||reg||5
Z||000002||Tigger||11-29-2001||02:58 PM||||Yes '85 to '87 is ribbed & rounded respectively.  They are different because a part of the trim is molded into the cover.  The overall shape and mounting is the same.<P>I can't remember if the '86 SE has rounded trim, if it does it will work.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||2
Z||000003||mrfiero||11-29-2001||03:36 PM||||The '84 Indy, '85 GT and '86-'87 SE all have the ribbed molding molded into the fascia.  Only the '86-'88 GT had the smooth molding (as far as the aero bodied Fieros go).<P>That said, you can install a "ribbed" fascia on a "smooth" car.  All it takes is a good sharpe utility knife to cut the small ribbed portion off.  Since the smooth sidemarker lights are longer than the ribbed ones this "void" is covered up when everything is installed.<P>E-mail me if you need help with what and where to cut.....I have done this numerous times.<P><BR> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||11-29-2001||03:36 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> Double post!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
