Z||000007||GT-maniac||11-30-2001||01:12 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AgaricX:<BR><B>Whats wrong with your fascia?  Is it cracked? Is it repairable?  I have an indy nose in good shape I'll trade you if the GT nose is salvageable.  I'm not going to use it anyway.<P>LMK<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks but the shipping cost from Texas to Canada would be prohibitive.<P>As for my nose I don't think it's really salvageable, the central support is ripped through, the side corners where it joins the fenders underneath the side marker lights are broken off. And the lower corners on each side underneath are simply gone. To top it off some genius decided to paint it with that rough paint that they spray box liners with. A nice rust brown color. Other than that there are no major rips. If your still interested I can dig it out of the snow and take some pics. If you want to pay shipping I can send it to you. Probably be pricy though unless I can find one locally I'll probably have to buy it from GM. At least they'll pay the shipping. <BR>BTW your convertible idea looks great, though I'm not crazy about the side scoops. Looks a little bit too mustangish to me.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero005a.jpg">  <P>85 WS6 GT partly modified<BR>87 GT Loaded resto project<p>[This message has been edited by GT-maniac (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||1
