Z||000012||88-DOHC||12-02-2001||02:23 AM||||There is some minor differences between the two noses. The most obvious is the molding that others have so pointed out.  The other is in some of the mounting hardware.  Either nose can be attached to any year/style Fiero, however you need to change out the inner honeycomb bumper material for the particular nose you are installing (yes, they are different).  Also the center paper-like air guides into the radiator that also attach to the nose, are different (the GT style has 3 screw attachments, and the coupe style only has 2 (per side)). The last thing is the front wheel wells have to be changed out. They also differ between GT and coupe nose.||||reg||1
Z||000013||mrfiero||12-02-2001||02:25 PM||||Good points, but he is not trying to swap a coupe nose for a GT nose.....he is trying to find out whether or not an '86 SE nose will work on his '87 GT.  The answer is yes, but some minor modifications need to be done to the SE nose.<P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000014||GT-maniac||12-03-2001||04:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88-DOHC:<BR><B>There is some minor differences between the two noses. The most obvious is the molding that others have so pointed out.  The other is in some of the mounting hardware.  Either nose can be attached to any year/style Fiero, however you need to change out the inner honeycomb bumper material for the particular nose you are installing (yes, they are different).  Also the center paper-like air guides into the radiator that also attach to the nose, are different (the GT style has 3 screw attachments, and the coupe style only has 2 (per side)). The last thing is the front wheel wells have to be changed out. They also differ between GT and coupe nose.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So the SE aero nose and a GT aero nose are different in the ways you've mentioned here then ?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||88-DOHC||12-03-2001||06:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GT-maniac:<BR><B> So the SE aero nose and a GT aero nose are different in the ways you've mentioned here then ?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The differences I outlined are the differences between GT style and coupe style noses. MrFiero jogged my brain and I rememebered that the SE came with a GT style nose (insert mental image of me slapping my forhead, DOH!). Basicly it was a coupe with a GT nose. So with respect to the SE and the GT noses, the only difference is the molding style, and a small portion of molding where the side marker light goes. The front side marker lights were shorter on the SE then the ones used on the GT. So there is a small amount of molding that would have to be removed from an SE nose since I believe its in conflict with the rear mounting hole for the GT side marker lights. Its been a while since I have looked at an SE nose compared to a GT so I may have forgotten something. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||JD86GT350||12-03-2001||07:34 PM||||the question has already been answered, but here's a visual for ya<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/frontcovers.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||cadaver||12-03-2001||08:13 PM||||And the holes for the badge are different. No big deal just drill what you need. But it is a difference and no one has mentioned it yet.||||reg||1
Z||000018||GT-maniac||12-03-2001||11:15 PM||||Thanks to everyone who replied to this topic. Looks like the putting on the SE nose won't be that big a deal. Funny thing is the nose I took off of the 87 GT doesn't have that piece molded into it and looks more like the SE nose in the picture. It's not the original nose though I don't think as the base color is different from the rest of the car. Maybe they changed the nose a bit when they went to the smooth moldings ? Anyway it doesn't matter as it should be fairly easy to modify the new SE nose to fit. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero005a.jpg">  <P>85 WS6 GT partly modified<BR>87 GT Loaded resto project<p>[This message has been edited by GT-maniac (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
